From 2c99c4641695a57583a8cbfb043fba49696cd433 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dingo <outbackdingo@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:26:08 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] harden: presence+non-empty+freshness checks for embedded
 kernel artifacts

The migration's silent risk was a kernel artifact that is deleted or stale and
nothing notices. Two gaps:

* titan-oxide-ffi/build.rs scanned image.rs line-by-line and took only the LAST
  quoted token per line; image.rs packs many embed!() calls onto one line, so of
  ~28 embedded artifacts only 2 were ever asserted.
* gemm's pinned PTX (gemm/gemm.ptx -> candle/candle-core/.../gemm_oxide.cubin) was
  covered by nothing at all.

Now every embed!() occurrence is checked; each artifact must exist and be
non-empty (hard error), is warned about when older than the crate source that
generates it, and the three libdevice-module PTX files (candle-reduce,
candle-unary, gemm) are asserted present and non-empty.

Adds oxide-kernels/PTX-PROVENANCE.md (the three libdevice crates emit NVVM IR and
no .ptx without libdevice.10.bc + llvm-link; the six crates that need nvcc-built
reference archives never built here) and check-artifact-freshness.sh (presence /
non-empty / freshness gate over every embedded artifact, the 11 candle ports and
the gemm copy; --strict fails on stale).
---
 PTX-PROVENANCE.md           | 78 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 check-artifact-freshness.sh | 77 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 titan-oxide-ffi/build.rs    | 57 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 209 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 PTX-PROVENANCE.md
 create mode 100755 check-artifact-freshness.sh

diff --git a/PTX-PROVENANCE.md b/PTX-PROVENANCE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3f0ea28
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PTX-PROVENANCE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,78 @@
+# PTX / cubin artifact provenance (per-crate)
+
+Committed artifacts in this repo are the **source of truth for the engine's embedded
+kernels**, but they are generated by a non-reproducible-on-this-box toolchain. This file
+records which crates cannot regenerate their own artifact here and what to do about it.
+
+## 1. Three crates emit NVVM IR, not PTX (libdevice modules)
+
+`candle-reduce`, `candle-unary`, `gemm` — and only these three — compile to a `.ll` plus
+`<stem>.options` + `<stem>.target` and **no `<stem>.ptx`**.
+
+Reason (upstream, in `cuda-oxide-codegen/src/pipeline.rs`): a module that uses strict
+CUDA-libdevice (`__nv_*`) calls is emitted as **NVVM IR** unless libdevice can be linked,
+and this box has neither `libdevice.10.bc` (no CUDA toolkit: `CUDA_HOME` is the `nocuda-bin`
+stub) nor a matching-LLVM-major `llvm-link`. The decision is
+`should_emit_nvvm_ir = uses_strict_libdevice && !can_ir_link_libdevice`, and that function is
+**byte-identical at `b9847e9` and at the `d141118c` tip** — this is not a migration
+regression. The build says so itself (build with `CUDA_OXIDE_VERBOSE=1`):
+
+```
+=== Detected CUDA libdevice (`__nv_*`) calls; auto-emitting NVVM IR (skip llc) ===
+=== Exporting to LLVM IR (NVVM IR mode) ===
+=== Skipping llc (libdevice present); consumer owns libNVVM/nvJitLink build ===
+```
+
+The only other crates with `.options`/`.target` sidecars are these three (the `NvvmIr`
+branch is the only writer of those files); every PTX-emitting crate has neither — use
+`ls */<stem>.target` as a quick discriminator.
+
+`cargo oxide inspect` on such a crate fails with
+`could not read generated PTX <dir>/<stem>.ptx: No such file or directory`.
+
+**Consequence:** the committed `<stem>.ptx` files are the pinned artifacts. `cargo oxide
+build` deletes them (`clean_generated_files`) and cannot recreate them here, so **after any
+`cargo oxide build` in these crates you must restore them**:
+
+```sh
+cd oxide-kernels
+git checkout -- candle-reduce/candle_reduce.ptx candle-unary/candle_unary.ptx gemm/gemm.ptx
+# and re-pin whatever consumes them:
+bash gemm/export.sh                 # gemm.ptx -> candle/candle-core/src/cuda_backend/gemm_oxide.ptx
+$CUDA_OXIDE_PTXAS -arch=sm_120 -O3 candle-reduce/candle_reduce.ptx -o /dev/null
+$CUDA_OXIDE_PTXAS -arch=sm_120 -O3 candle-unary/candle_unary.ptx  -o /dev/null
+```
+
+To make these crates emit PTX again instead, provide both `libdevice.10.bc` and a matching
+`llvm-link` (a real CUDA toolkit, or `CUDA_OXIDE_LIBDEVICE` + `CUDA_OXIDE_LLVM_LINK`).
+
+Caveat: the pinned PTX was produced where libdevice *was* available (its `__nv_*` calls are
+already lowered to native instructions — no `.extern .func __nv_*` survives), so it is
+self-contained and loads without a libdevice JIT step.
+
+## 2. Six crates cannot build on a CUDA-toolkit-free box (nvcc reference archives)
+
+`mistralrs-core-cuda`, `mistralrs-paged-attn-a`, `mistralrs-paged-attn-b`,
+`mistralrs-quant-a`, `mistralrs-quant-b`, `mistralrs-quant-c`.
+
+Their `build.rs` needs the nvcc-built C **reference** static archives and panics/links-fails
+without them:
+
+| crate | archive (missing) |
+|---|---|
+| mistralrs-core-cuda   | `reference/mistralrs-core/libmistralrscuda.a` |
+| mistralrs-paged-attn-a/b | `reference/mistralrs-paged-attn{-094,}/libmistralrspagedattention.a` |
+| mistralrs-quant-a/c   | `reference/mistralrs-quant/libmistralrsquant.a` |
+| mistralrs-quant-b     | `reference/mistralrs-quant/libmistralrsquant.a` (+ `-lcudart -lstdc++` at link) |
+
+These `.a` files are `.gitignore`d (`reference/*/lib*.a`), have **never** been committed (no
+`.a` was ever added in this repo's history) and are not present on this box. They are the
+product of an nvcc reference build, which this fork's nvcc-free path deliberately cannot run.
+The migration touched only `Cargo.toml` in these crates, so this is **pre-existing, not a
+migration regression** — they did not build before the pin move either.
+
+## 3. Freshness gate
+
+`./check-artifact-freshness.sh` verifies that every artifact embedded by `titan-oxide-ffi`
+and by `candle-kernels` exists, is non-empty, and is not older than the crate source that
+produces it. Run it before publishing an engine build.
diff --git a/check-artifact-freshness.sh b/check-artifact-freshness.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..aece98f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/check-artifact-freshness.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+# Guard against silently shipping a missing, empty or stale kernel artifact.
+#
+# Every kernel the engine embeds is a *committed* file in this repo, generated by a build that
+# can no longer be reproduced on this box (see PTX-PROVENANCE.md). `cargo oxide build` deletes
+# them and, for the three libdevice modules, cannot recreate them; nothing about a later engine
+# build would notice a *stale* one at all. So check before publishing.
+#
+#   ./check-artifact-freshness.sh              MISSING/EMPTY fail; STALE warns (exit 0)
+#   ./check-artifact-freshness.sh --strict     STALE also fails
+#
+# A STALE row means the artifact is older than <crate>/src/main.rs: rebuild the crate and, when
+# it has no PTX (see PTX-PROVENANCE.md), restore the pinned file with `git checkout --`.
+set -uo pipefail
+
+HERE=$(cd "$(dirname "$(readlink -f "$0")")" && pwd)
+STRICT=0; [ "${1:-}" = "--strict" ] && STRICT=1
+IMAGE=$HERE/titan-oxide-ffi/src/image.rs
+fail=0; warn=0
+
+row() { # $1=status $2=artifact-rel $3=source-rel
+  printf '%-7s %-56s %s\n' "$1" "$2" "${3:-}"
+}
+
+mtime_of() { stat -c %Y "$1" 2>/dev/null || echo 0; }
+
+check() { # $1=artifact-rel $2=source-rel
+  local a=$HERE/$1 s=$HERE/$2
+  if [ ! -f "$a" ]; then row MISSING "$1" "expected from $2"; fail=1; return; fi
+  if [ ! -s "$a" ]; then row EMPTY "$1" "0 bytes"; fail=1; return; fi
+  if [ ! -f "$s" ]; then row OK "$1" "(source $2 absent)"; return; fi
+  if [ "$(mtime_of "$a")" -lt "$(mtime_of "$s")" ]; then
+    row STALE "$1" "older than $2"; warn=1
+  else
+    row OK "$1" ""
+  fi
+}
+
+echo "== artifacts embedded by titan-oxide-ffi (titan-oxide-ffi/src/image.rs) =="
+# every embed!(name,\"sym\",\"path\") path, not one per source line
+mapfile -t EMBED < <(grep -oE 'embed!\([^)]*\)' "$IMAGE" | sed -E 's/.*,\s*"([^"]+)"\).*/\1/')
+for rel in "${EMBED[@]}"; do
+  [ -n "$rel" ] || continue
+  case "$rel" in
+    mistralrs-quant-b/marlin-kernels/*) src=mistralrs-quant-b/marlin-kernels/src/main.rs ;;
+    */*/) src=${rel%/*/*}/src/main.rs ;;      # one nested level
+    *)    src=${rel%%/*}/src/main.rs ;;
+  esac
+  check "$rel" "$src"
+done
+
+echo
+echo "== candle modules materialized by candle-kernels/build.rs (TITAN_OXIDE_DIR ports) =="
+for m in affine binary cast conv fill indexing quantized reduce sort ternary unary; do
+  check "candle-$m/candle_$m.ptx" "candle-$m/src/main.rs"
+done
+
+echo
+echo "== gemm: pinned PTX and the engine's copy must agree =="
+G=$HERE/gemm/gemm.ptx
+C=$HERE/../candle/candle-core/src/cuda_backend/gemm_oxide.ptx
+if [ -f "$G" ] && [ -f "$C" ]; then
+  if cmp -s "$G" "$C"; then row OK "gemm/gemm.ptx == .../gemm_oxide.ptx" ""
+  else row STALE "gemm/gemm.ptx != .../gemm_oxide.ptx" "run: bash gemm/export.sh"; warn=1; fi
+else row MISSING "gemm/gemm.ptx or gemm_oxide.ptx" ""; fail=1; fi
+
+echo
+echo "== libdevice modules: a PTX-emitting build needs libdevice + llvm-link =="
+for c in candle-reduce candle-unary gemm; do
+  printf 'note    %-20s emits NVVM IR + no .ptx unless libdevice.10.bc and llvm-link exist\n' "$c"
+done
+
+echo
+if [ "$fail" = 1 ]; then echo "RESULT: FAIL (missing or empty artifact)"; exit 1; fi
+if [ "$warn" = 1 ] && [ "$STRICT" = 1 ]; then echo "RESULT: FAIL (stale artifact, --strict)"; exit 1; fi
+if [ "$warn" = 1 ]; then echo "RESULT: OK (with stale warnings)"; exit 0; fi
+echo "RESULT: OK"; exit 0
diff --git a/titan-oxide-ffi/build.rs b/titan-oxide-ffi/build.rs
index 069e7d1..e502946 100644
--- a/titan-oxide-ffi/build.rs
+++ b/titan-oxide-ffi/build.rs
@@ -21,18 +21,69 @@ fn main() {
         println!("cargo:rustc-cfg=has_ref");
     }
     println!("cargo:rustc-check-cfg=cfg(has_ref)");
+    // The PTX tail: a card that exists on no generation list yet runs the module by JIT,
+    // one JIT per module (measured 3-72 s; see m4/nojit/README.md). Off by default, so the
+    // shipped binary carries cubins only.
+    println!("cargo:rerun-if-env-changed=TITAN_EMBED_PTX_TAIL");
+    if std::env::var_os("TITAN_EMBED_PTX_TAIL").is_some() {
+        println!("cargo:rustc-cfg=oxide_ptx_tail");
+    }
+    println!("cargo:rustc-check-cfg=cfg(oxide_ptx_tail)");
     for l in libs {
         println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed={dir}/lib{l}.a");
     }
     // The PTX embedded by src/image.rs (`.incbin`, invisible to rustc's dependency tracking).
+    //
+    // Every `embed!` occurrence is checked, not one per source line: image.rs packs many calls
+    // onto a single line, so a line-based scan only ever saw the last one on each line — the
+    // hole that let deleted artifacts go unnoticed. See PTX-PROVENANCE.md.
     let manifest = env!("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR");
     let image = std::fs::read_to_string(format!("{manifest}/src/image.rs")).unwrap();
-    for line in image.lines().filter(|l| l.starts_with("embed!(")) {
-        let path = line.rsplit('"').nth(1).unwrap();
+    let mtime = |p: &str| {
+        std::fs::metadata(p)
+            .and_then(|m| m.modified())
+            .unwrap_or(std::time::SystemTime::UNIX_EPOCH)
+    };
+    let mut checked = 0usize;
+    for chunk in image.split("embed!(").skip(1) {
+        // The path is the last quoted token of the call, exactly as the old line-scanner read
+        // it — only the "one occurrence per line" restriction is dropped.
+        let Some(path) = chunk.rsplit('"').nth(1) else {
+            continue;
+        };
         let full = format!("{manifest}/../{path}");
-        assert!(std::path::Path::new(&full).exists(), "embedded PTX missing: {full}");
+        let meta = std::fs::metadata(&full)
+            .unwrap_or_else(|_| panic!("embedded kernel artifact missing: {full}"));
+        assert!(meta.len() > 0, "embedded kernel artifact is empty: {full}");
+        checked += 1;
+        // Freshness: an artifact older than the crate source that generates it was not
+        // regenerated (or exported) after the source changed. A warning, not a failure: some
+        // artifacts predate this check, and `check-artifact-freshness.sh` is the strict gate.
+        if let Some(crate_dir) = std::path::Path::new(path).parent() {
+            let src = format!("{manifest}/../{}/src/main.rs", crate_dir.display());
+            if std::path::Path::new(&src).exists() && mtime(&full) < mtime(&src) {
+                println!("cargo::warning=titan: STALE embedded artifact {path} is older than {src}");
+            }
+        }
+        println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed={full}");
+    }
+    // The three libdevice modules (candle-reduce, candle-unary, gemm) emit NVVM IR and no `.ptx`
+    // on a box without libdevice.10.bc + llvm-link, so their committed `.ptx` is the pinned
+    // artifact. candle-kernels/build.rs already panics on a missing reduce/unary port; gemm's
+    // pinned file is not covered anywhere else, and these are invisible to rustc's tracking.
+    for pinned in [
+        "candle-reduce/candle_reduce.ptx",
+        "candle-unary/candle_unary.ptx",
+        "gemm/gemm.ptx",
+    ] {
+        let full = format!("{manifest}/../{pinned}");
+        let meta = std::fs::metadata(&full).unwrap_or_else(|_| {
+            panic!("pinned libdevice-module PTX missing; restore it with `git checkout -- {pinned}`: {full}")
+        });
+        assert!(!meta.is_file() || meta.len() > 0, "pinned libdevice-module PTX is empty: {full}");
         println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed={full}");
     }
+    let _ = checked;
     println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed=src/image.rs");
     println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed=build.rs");
 }
