From 1dd52c3fe84dd47c2be5715b425be33f9f0287eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dingo <outbackdingo@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:48:02 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] docs+gate: record the batch-delete trap and print the
 restore recipe
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A full `cargo oxide build` batch (39 crates) left 12 tracked artifacts deleted —
the six crates that cannot build here delete their committed .cubin/.ptx and put
nothing back — and also removed two gitignored native cubins
(flash-prefill/flash_prefill.cubin, flash-decode/flash_decode.cubin) that cannot
be `git checkout`ed. check-artifact-freshness.sh caught all of it as MISSING.

Documents both in PTX-PROVENANCE.md §4 with the exact restore commands, and makes
the gate print those commands on failure.
---
 PTX-PROVENANCE.md           | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 check-artifact-freshness.sh | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 41 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/PTX-PROVENANCE.md b/PTX-PROVENANCE.md
index 3f0ea28..b60fbe5 100644
--- a/PTX-PROVENANCE.md
+++ b/PTX-PROVENANCE.md
@@ -76,3 +76,27 @@ migration regression** — they did not build before the pin move either.
 `./check-artifact-freshness.sh` verifies that every artifact embedded by `titan-oxide-ffi`
 and by `candle-kernels` exists, is non-empty, and is not older than the crate source that
 produces it. Run it before publishing an engine build.
+
+## 4. A batch build deletes artifacts, and some cannot be restored from git
+
+`cargo oxide build` calls `clean_generated_files` first, so **every** `<stem>.ptx`, `.ll`,
+`.cubin`, `.target`, `.options` goes away and is only re-created if the build succeeds. Two
+consequences seen in practice:
+
+- Building a crate that *cannot* build here (§2) deletes its committed `.cubin`/`.ptx` and
+  puts nothing back. After a batch this repo can be left with a dozen tracked deletions —
+  `git status --short | grep '^ D'`. Restore them with
+  `git checkout -- $(git diff --name-only --diff-filter=D)`.
+- Some native cubins are **not** in git (`*.cubin` is ignored): `flash-prefill/flash_prefill.cubin`
+  and `flash-decode/flash_decode.cubin` in particular. A batch build removes them and they
+  cannot be `git checkout`ed back. Re-assemble them with the crate's own `.target`:
+
+  ```sh
+  for p in flash-prefill/flash_prefill flash-decode/flash_decode; do
+    t=$(grep -m1 '^\.target' $p.ptx | awk '{print $2}')
+    "$CUDA_OXIDE_PTXAS" -arch="$t" -O3 $p.ptx -o $p.cubin
+  done
+  ```
+
+`check-artifact-freshness.sh` reports both situations as `MISSING`; run it (and the restore
+steps) after any batch build, before rebuilding the engine.
